ASPIRATIONAL — tree-store TT1 (parent synthesis) + TT5 (forest preorder). NOT built yet.

This is the FIRST acceptance red of the [tree]-store spec (see ../DESIGN.md). It
sits on the LANDED self-FK substrate (690_048): parent is a synthesized i64
self-FK, -1 = root, set via the real `stored { tree[c].parent: p }` write.

Missing surface, in the order the compiler will surface it:
  1. std/store:preorder(name) / `! preorder { ... }` — the DFS pre-order walk.
     Current wall: `error[KORU040]: unknown event 'std.store:preorder'`.
  2. `[tree]` annotation must actually SYNTHESIZE the `parent` column + wire the
     traversal API. Today `[tree]` parses but is a silent no-op; the `parent`
     writes compile only because field validation hasn't rejected them (watch
     this when building — a write to an unsynthesized `parent` should error).

Expected output once built (DFS pre-order of root(10) → a(20) → c(40) → b(30)):
  10 / 20 / 40 / 30   (NOT insertion/BFS 10 20 30 40 — 40-before-30 proves preorder)
